  "description": "meme-id: black_people_anthing_that_doesnt_belong_to_them; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman holding a rusty, worn-out funnel, with text overlaying the image that reads 'black people' at the top and 'anthing that doesn't belong to them' at the bottom. The visual of the funnel, combined with the text, is an analogical mapping that implies Black people are undeserving of certain things or are being denied access to them. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that reduces a racial group to a metaphorical object of exclusion and dispossession. The meme uses racist tropes to dehumanize and demean Black people by suggesting they are inherently unworthy of ownership or possession, which is a direct attack based on race. The intent is to perpetuate racial prejudice and reinforce systemic exclusion through visual and textual juxtaposition.",
